{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-L19-server-database-3-01","date":"2026-11-21","lens":"19","surface":"server","area":"server/database-3","refs":["F-server-512","F-server-533"],"severity":"S4","title":"Giving back a counted AI question needs no proof that our web server asked","what":"Taking an AI question from a gym's credits must be signed by our web server, but giving one back (after a failed answer) is open to anyone with the public app key and only needs the question's id. A given-back question no longer counts against the member's or visitor's daily limit, the gym's daily limit or the owner's monthly limit, and its slot returns to the credit block. Today the id stays inside our web server, so nobody outside can use it; the safety rests on that id never leaking.","expected":"Only our web server can give a question back, signed the same way as taking one.","evidence":["supabase/migrations/0083_ai_members.sql:199-213","supabase/migrations/0083_ai_members.sql:273-277","supabase/migrations/0078_ai_questions.sql:221-230","deploy/panel/questionCredits.js:93-101"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"question-give-back-not-signed","who":"owners","how_often":"only if a question id ever leaks","fix_line":"Sign the give-back with the same server secret as the take, and stop the public app key calling it","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
